content:
NOTE: This is a working draft intended to unblock control-plane storage + policy evaluation integration. Not a final public contract.

Context
- Optimize proposes config deltas (batching/caching/quantization/routing) that can impact output quality.
- Control plane must gate “apply” using eval-harness results + thresholds.
- We need a versioned, auditable policy schema with:
  - per-route thresholds
  - per-tenant overrides
  - version pinning to models + prompt sets + threshold bundles

Design goals
1) Deterministic decisions: same inputs => same pass/fail.
2) Auditability: we can reconstruct “what policy + thresholds + suites were used” after the fact.
3) Safe rollouts: observe-only -> soft-block -> hard-block; policy changes can be staged.
4) Minimal cardinality: avoid exploding metric labels; keep high-cardinality fields in artifacts, not telemetry.

Non-goals (for this schema)
- Defining the eval output format in detail (owned by eval-harness). We only reference expected fields.
- Modeling all future policy types. This schema should be extensible.

Terminology
- GuardrailPolicy: top-level object stored in control plane (versioned).
- ThresholdBundle: reusable set of thresholds by workload/model family/metric.
- Prompt set revision: immutable identifier for prompt set content (hash or monotonic rev).
- Model version: Redwood model identifier with immutable build/version (e.g., llama-3.1-70b-instruct@2025-01-09.1).

===========================
1) Top-level object: GuardrailPolicy
===========================

Pseudo-schema (not full JSON Schema spec; types shown as comments)
{
  "kind": "GuardrailPolicy",                              // string, fixed
  "schema_version": "2025-01-guardrails.v1",             // string

  "policy_id": "grp_...",                                // string (stable id)
  "policy_version": "1.3.0",                             // string (semver-ish)
  "status": "draft|active|deprecated",                   // string

  "created_at": "2025-01-10T19:42:00Z",                  // string (RFC3339)
  "created_by": "user_...",                              // string (principal id)
  "last_modified_at": "2025-01-22T03:15:22Z",            // string
  "last_modified_by": "user_...",                        // string

  "description": "...",                                  // string
  "notes": "...",                                        // string (freeform)

  "rollout": {
    "enforcement_mode": "observe_only|soft_block|hard_block",  // string
    "soft_block": {
      "allow_override": true,                               // bool
      "override_policy_id": "ovr_..."                      // string
    },
    "tenant_rollout": {
      "default": "observe_only",                           // string
      "by_tier": {
        "free": "observe_only",
        "pro": "soft_block",
        "enterprise": "hard_block"
      },
      "allowlist_tenants": ["tnt_..."],                    // list[string]
      "blocklist_tenants": ["tnt_..."]                     // list[string]
    }
  },

  "pins": {
    "threshold_bundle_ref": "thb_...@2.1.0",              // string (id@version)
    "suite_bundle_ref": "srb_...@1.0.0",                  // string (id@version)

    "prompt_set": {
      "source": "redwood|customer",                       // string
      "prompt_set_id": "pset_...",                        // string
      "prompt_set_revision": "rev_2025-01-18_9d3f..."      // string (immutable)
    },

    "model_pinning": {
      "mode": "model_version|model_family",               // string
      "model_versions": ["llama-3.1-70b-instruct@2025-01-09.1"], // list[string]
      "model_families": ["llama-3.x"],                     // list[string]
      "allow_unpinned_models": false                        // bool
    }
  },

  "matchers": [
    {
      "matcher_id": "m_chat_default",                     // string
      "route": {"type": "exact", "value": "/v1/chat/completions"},     // object
      "workload_tags": ["chat", "tool_calling"],         // list[string]
      "optimization_types": ["batching", "caching", "quantization", "routing"], // list[string]
      "customer_tiers": ["pro", "enterprise"],           // list[string]

      "eval_selection": {
        "selector": "by_optimization_type",               // string
        "suites": ["safety_smoke", "format_strict", "task_success_rubric"], // list[string]
        "min_prompts": 200,                                 // number
        "max_eval_seconds": 900,                             // number
        "rerun_on_flake": {"enabled": true, "max_reruns": 1} // object
      },

      "thresholds": {
        "threshold_profile": "default",                   // string (key into ThresholdBundle)
        "overrides": [
          {
            "metric": "task_success",                      // string
            "aggregation": "mean",                          // string
            "comparison": "delta_vs_baseline",              // string
            "direction": "lower_is_worse",                  // string
            "max_regression": "-0.010",                     // string for stable formatting in audit logs
            "min_sample_size": "150",                       // string
            "ci": {"method": "bootstrap", "alpha": "0.05"} // object
          }
        ]
      },

      "actions_on_failure": {
        "default_action": "block_apply",                   // string
        "failure_categories": {
          "eval_timeout": "block_apply",
          "eval_error": "block_apply",
          "threshold_fail": "block_apply"
        }
      }
    }
  ],

  "tenants": {
    "overrides": [
      {
        "tenant_id": "tnt_...",                           // string
        "mode": "merge|replace",                          // string
        "notes": "...",
        "matcher_overrides": [
          {
            "matcher_id": "m_chat_default",
            "thresholds": {
              "overrides": [
                {"metric": "format_valid_json", "comparison": "min_value", "min_value": "0.995"}
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

Implementation notes
- We store all timestamps/ids as strings to keep the serialized payload stable.
- Numbers inside threshold rules are stored as strings in this draft to avoid inconsistent float formatting across services. Policy engine should parse them into decimals.
- “matchers” are evaluated in order; first match wins (or optionally: “all matches apply” — TBD, see Open questions).


===========================
2) ThresholdBundle (referenced by GuardrailPolicy.pins.threshold_bundle_ref)
===========================

Intent: A reusable, versioned library of metric thresholds keyed by workload type + model family.

Draft object
{
  "kind": "ThresholdBundle",
  "schema_version": "2025-01-guardrails-thresholds.v1",

  "bundle_id": "thb_default",
  "bundle_version": "2.1.0",

  "description": "Default guardrails thresholds used by Optimize gating",

  "profiles": {
    "default": {
      "workload": "chat",
      "rules": [
        {
          "metric": "task_success",
          "aggregation": "mean",
          "comparison": "delta_vs_baseline",
          "direction": "lower_is_worse",
          "max_regression": "-0.010",
          "min_sample_size": "150",
          "ci": {"method": "bootstrap", "alpha": "0.05"}
        },
        {
          "metric": "toxicity_rate",
          "aggregation": "mean",
          "comparison": "max_value",
          "max_value": "0.002",
          "min_sample_size": "200",
          "ci": {"method": "wilson", "alpha": "0.05"}
        },
        {
          "metric": "format_valid_json",
          "aggregation": "mean",
          "comparison": "min_value",
          "min_value": "0.990",
          "min_sample_size": "120",
          "ci": {"method": "wilson", "alpha": "0.05"}
        }
      ],

      "model_family_adjustments": [
        {
          "model_family": "llama-3.x",
          "rule_overrides": [
            {"metric": "task_success", "max_regression": "-0.008"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "model_family": "qwen2.x",
          "rule_overrides": [
            {"metric": "format_valid_json", "min_value": "0.995"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "quantization_strict": {
      "workload": "chat",
      "rules": [
        {"metric": "task_success", "comparison": "delta_vs_baseline", "max_regression": "-0.005", "min_sample_size": "250", "ci": {"method": "bootstrap", "alpha": "0.05"}},
        {"metric": "reasoning_rubric", "comparison": "delta_vs_baseline", "max_regression": "-0.010", "min_sample_size": "200", "ci": {"method": "bootstrap", "alpha": "0.05"}},
        {"metric": "format_valid_json", "comparison": "min_value", "min_value": "0.995", "min_sample_size": "200", "ci": {"method": "wilson", "alpha": "0.05"}}
      ]
    }
  }
}

Note: “model_family_adjustments” is preferred over per-model-version thresholds in the bundle. Actual model version pinning should happen in GuardrailPolicy.pins.model_pinning.


===========================
3) SuiteBundle (referenced by GuardrailPolicy.pins.suite_bundle_ref)
===========================

We need a stable mapping from optimization type -> suite list (so changes are auditable and don’t drift with code changes).

{
  "kind": "SuiteBundle",
  "schema_version": "2025-01-guardrails-suites.v1",

  "bundle_id": "srb_optimize_gating",
  "bundle_version": "1.0.0",

  "suites": {
    "batching": ["format_strict", "task_success_rubric"],
    "caching": ["format_strict", "factuality_proxy", "task_success_rubric"],
    "quantization": ["format_strict", "reasoning_rubric", "task_success_rubric", "safety_smoke"],
    "routing": ["task_success_rubric", "safety_smoke"]
  },

  "workload_tags": {
    "tool_calling": ["tool_args_valid", "tool_choice_correct"],
    "structured_output": ["format_valid_json", "schema_conformance"]
  }
}


===========================
4) Overrides / approval model
===========================

We expect overrides only in soft-block (and possibly enterprise hard-block w/ break-glass).

OverridePolicy (referenced by GuardrailPolicy.rollout.soft_block.override_policy_id)
{
  "kind": "OverridePolicy",
  "schema_version": "2025-01-override.v1",

  "override_policy_id": "ovr_default",
  "override_policy_version": "1.0.0",

  "requirements": {
    "justification_required": true,
    "justification_min_chars": "30",
    "max_overrides_per_tenant_per_day": "3",
    "requires_second_approver": true,
    "approver_roles": ["platform_oncall", "security_oncall", "customer_success_manager"],
    "requestor_roles": ["tenant_admin", "platform_oncall"]
  },

  "audit": {
    "emit_audit_event": true,
    "event_type": "OptimizeConfigChange",
    "retain_days": "365"
  }
}

Notes
- Second approver requirement is contentious; keep it configurable per tier.
- Platform oncall should be able to do break-glass for production incidents, but must provide a reason and link to incident/ticket.


===========================
5) Example policies
===========================

Example A: Default policy for /v1/chat/completions
{
  "kind": "GuardrailPolicy",
  "schema_version": "2025-01-guardrails.v1",

  "policy_id": "grp_optimize_default",
  "policy_version": "1.3.0",
  "status": "active",

  "created_at": "2025-01-10T19:42:00Z",
  "created_by": "user_bokafor",
  "last_modified_at": "2025-01-22T03:15:22Z",
  "last_modified_by": "user_jlee",

  "description": "Default Optimize gating policy (chat/tool calling)",
  "notes": "Pinned to threshold bundle + suite bundle; prompt set rev updated for pilot.",

  "rollout": {
    "enforcement_mode": "soft_block",
    "soft_block": {"allow_override": true, "override_policy_id": "ovr_default"},
    "tenant_rollout": {
      "default": "observe_only",
      "by_tier": {"free": "observe_only", "pro": "soft_block", "enterprise": "soft_block"},
      "allowlist_tenants": ["tnt_design_partner_1049921"],
      "blocklist_tenants": []
    }
  },

  "pins": {
    "threshold_bundle_ref": "thb_default@2.1.0",
    "suite_bundle_ref": "srb_optimize_gating@1.0.0",
    "prompt_set": {"source": "redwood", "prompt_set_id": "pset_optimize_guardrails", "prompt_set_revision": "rev_2025-01-18_9d3f1a"},
    "model_pinning": {"mode": "model_family", "model_versions": [], "model_families": ["llama-3.x", "qwen2.x"], "allow_unpinned_models": false}
  },

  "matchers": [
    {
      "matcher_id": "m_chat_default",
      "route": {"type": "exact", "value": "/v1/chat/completions"},
      "workload_tags": ["chat"],
      "optimization_types": ["batching", "caching", "routing"],
      "customer_tiers": ["pro", "enterprise"],

      "eval_selection": {"selector": "by_optimization_type", "suites": ["format_strict", "task_success_rubric"], "min_prompts": 200, "max_eval_seconds": 900, "rerun_on_flake": {"enabled": true, "max_reruns": 1}},

      "thresholds": {"threshold_profile": "default", "overrides": []},

      "actions_on_failure": {"default_action": "block_apply", "failure_categories": {"eval_timeout": "block_apply", "eval_error": "block_apply", "threshold_fail": "block_apply"}}
    },

    {
      "matcher_id": "m_chat_quant",
      "route": {"type": "exact", "value": "/v1/chat/completions"},
      "workload_tags": ["chat"],
      "optimization_types": ["quantization"],
      "customer_tiers": ["pro", "enterprise"],

      "eval_selection": {"selector": "by_optimization_type", "suites": ["format_strict", "reasoning_rubric", "task_success_rubric", "safety_smoke"], "min_prompts": 250, "max_eval_seconds": 1200, "rerun_on_flake": {"enabled": true, "max_reruns": 1}},

      "thresholds": {"threshold_profile": "quantization_strict", "overrides": []},

      "actions_on_failure": {"default_action": "block_apply", "failure_categories": {"eval_timeout": "block_apply", "eval_error": "block_apply", "threshold_fail": "block_apply"}}
    }
  ],

  "tenants": {"overrides": []}
}


Example B: Tenant override (Acme FinTech) — stricter formatting + no override
{
  "kind": "GuardrailPolicy",
  "schema_version": "2025-01-guardrails.v1",

  "policy_id": "grp_optimize_default",
  "policy_version": "1.3.0",
  "status": "active",

  "created_at": "2025-01-10T19:42:00Z",
  "created_by": "user_bokafor",
  "last_modified_at": "2025-01-22T03:15:22Z",
  "last_modified_by": "user_jlee",

  "description": "Default Optimize gating policy (chat/tool calling)",
  "notes": "Tenant override appended for high-sensitivity tenant. (In storage, tenant overrides may be separate objects; this shows logical structure.)",

  "rollout": {
    "enforcement_mode": "soft_block",
    "soft_block": {"allow_override": true, "override_policy_id": "ovr_default"},
    "tenant_rollout": {"default": "observe_only", "by_tier": {"free": "observe_only", "pro": "soft_block", "enterprise": "soft_block"}, "allowlist_tenants": ["tnt_design_partner_1049921"], "blocklist_tenants": []}
  },

  "pins": {
    "threshold_bundle_ref": "thb_default@2.1.0",
    "suite_bundle_ref": "srb_optimize_gating@1.0.0",
    "prompt_set": {"source": "customer", "prompt_set_id": "pset_acme_fintech", "prompt_set_revision": "rev_2025-01-20_38ac09"},
    "model_pinning": {"mode": "model_version", "model_versions": ["llama-3.1-70b-instruct@2025-01-09.1"], "model_families": [], "allow_unpinned_models": false}
  },

  "matchers": [
    {
      "matcher_id": "m_chat_default",
      "route": {"type": "exact", "value": "/v1/chat/completions"},
      "workload_tags": ["chat", "structured_output"],
      "optimization_types": ["batching", "caching", "routing", "quantization"],
      "customer_tiers": ["enterprise"],
      "eval_selection": {"selector": "by_optimization_type", "suites": ["schema_conformance", "format_strict", "task_success_rubric", "safety_smoke"], "min_prompts": 300, "max_eval_seconds": 1800, "rerun_on_flake": {"enabled": true, "max_reruns": 1}},
      "thresholds": {
        "threshold_profile": "quantization_strict",
        "overrides": [
          {"metric": "format_valid_json", "aggregation": "mean", "comparison": "min_value", "min_value": "0.998", "min_sample_size": "300", "ci": {"method": "wilson", "alpha": "0.05"}}
        ]
      },
      "actions_on_failure": {"default_action": "block_apply", "failure_categories": {"eval_timeout": "block_apply", "eval_error": "block_apply", "threshold_fail": "block_apply"}}
    }
  ],

  "tenants": {
    "overrides": [
      {
        "tenant_id": "tnt_acme_fintech_1049921",
        "mode": "merge",
        "notes": "Acme does not want human overrides for quality gates; requires strict formatting compliance.",
        "matcher_overrides": [
          {
            "matcher_id": "m_chat_default",
            "thresholds": {"overrides": [{"metric": "format_valid_json", "comparison": "min_value", "min_value": "0.998"}]}
          }
        ],
        "override_behavior": {"allow_override": false}
      }
    ]
  }
}


===========================
6) Storage & versioning expectations (control plane)
===========================

- Policy versions are immutable once status=active.
- Updates create a new policy_version and optionally deprecate the old.
- Tenants should have an “effective policy reference” recorded at apply-time:
  - policy_id@policy_version
  - threshold_bundle_ref
  - suite_bundle_ref
  - prompt_set_id@prompt_set_revision
  - model pin (exact model version used for eval)

Audit event must capture the “effective” references above (not just latest pointers).


===========================
7) Open questions / TODO
===========================

1) Matcher evaluation semantics
- First-match-wins vs merge-all-matches. First-match is simpler + deterministic. Merge-all is flexible but can be surprising.

2) How to represent baseline
- Baseline is currently: “existing config on the route” at apply-time (or last-known good). Need to encode baseline source in apply request + audit.

3) Prompt set pinning strategy
- For Redwood-managed prompt sets, do we allow “latest” pointers? Applied ML prefers immutable rev pinning for gating.

4) Numeric encoding
- Keeping numeric thresholds as strings simplifies audit stability but is awkward. Alternative: allow numbers and normalize formatting in control-plane serializer.

5) Tenant overrides as separate object
- Might be cleaner to store TenantGuardrailOverrides separately to avoid rewriting large policies. This draft shows them inline for readability.

6) Failure category taxonomy
- Need agreement with SRE/UI on how many categories we surface: timeout vs infra error vs threshold failure vs invalid config.

Contact / owners
- Schema + persistence: Benji Okafor, Michael Nguyen
- Policy evaluation semantics: Jordan Lee
- Threshold methodology: Selene Huang, Sana Farid
- Audit/RBAC constraints: Naomi Feldman
